# Tayam, Luminous Enigma's "{3}, Remove three counters from among creatures you control" (CR 118.3, 602.2b). On turn 5 Bot1's
# creatures have two counters (Ornithopter's and Birds of Paradise's vigilance counters); its Chalice of the Void's two charge
# counters are not on a creature, and Bot2's Walking Ballista's +1/+1 counter is not on a creature Bot1 controls. So with four
# mana open the ability can't be activated - one short under the right reading, enough under either wrong one. On turn 7
# Llanowar Elves enters with a third, and the ability is activated for exactly {3}: three Moxen tapped, nothing left in the
# pool, Mox Sapphire untapped. The counters come off the three creatures and the Chalice keeps its two. The mill finds three
# Lightning Bolts, none a permanent card, so nothing returns.

